[Better Approach 2] Bottom-Up DP - O(n * m * L) Time and O(n) Space The idea is to use bottom-up dynamic programming to check if the string can be broken into dictionary words. Create a boolean array dp[] of size n + 1, where dp[i] is true if the prefix s[0..i) can be broken into dictionary words.Working of the Approach:Mark dp[0] = true, as an empty prefix is always valid (base case).For each position i from 1 to n, check every dictionary word that ends at position i.If such a word starts at a position j where dp[j] is true, then dp[i] = true.At the end, return dp[n].
            C++

    #include <iostream>
using namespace std;

bool wordBreak(string &s, vector<string> &dictionary)
{
    int n = s.size();
    vector<bool> dp(n + 1, 0);
    dp[0] = 1;

    // Traverse through the given string
    for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++)
    {

        // Traverse through the dictionary words
        for (string &w : dictionary)
        {

            // Check if current word is present
            // the prefix before the word is also
            // breakable
            int start = i - w.size();
            if (start >= 0 && dp[start] && s.substr(start, w.size()) == w)
            {
                dp[i] = 1;
                break;
            }
        }
    }
    return dp[n];
}

